{
  "commit_id": "dbe647efed4afd241296d87076577629bfd4e13a",
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "body": "Thanks for the contribution — this is a really helpful addition for #36 and the hardening checklist will be useful for self-hosters. A few small factual fixes below; happy to merge once those are addressed.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "SECURITY.md",
      "line": 77,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "Small factual fix: simple-mode is not activated by `USE_SIMPLE_MODE=true` — that env var only appears in the `server_simple.py` docstring and is not read anywhere at runtime. `make dev` uses simple-mode because the Dockerfile CMD is `python server_simple.py` (no compose/Makefile env gate). Suggest rephrasing to something like: *\"runs `server_simple.py` (default via `make dev` / Docker image CMD)\"*."
    },
    {
      "path": "SECURITY.md",
      "line": 100,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "The loopback binding example uses `127.0.0.1:8000:8000`, but our default `docker-compose.yml` maps **`8001:8000`** (see `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`). Could you update to `127.0.0.1:8001:8000` so it matches `make dev`? (Container port 8000 in the table above is fine.)"
    },
    {
      "path": "SECURITY.md",
      "line": 132,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "This bullet is not accurate for simple-mode: `server_simple.py`'s `InvestigateRequest` has no size `Field` constraints (unlike `server.py`, which caps prompt/images via Pydantic). Today body limits are proxy-only. Suggest dropping this bullet or rephrasing as a proxy-layer responsibility only."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "commit_id": "3c2002a2a9d0b3102b0b521a48bace2f3c5bd192",
  "event": "APPROVE",
  "body": "Thanks for fixing this — the `/answer` false-success bug was real and this is a clean, well-scoped fix for #20.\n\nValidated locally: merges cleanly onto current `main` (merge and rebase both work), `ruff check` on changed files passes, and the full `sre-agent` unit suite is green aside from 3 pre-existing Helm dependency test failures on `main`. Good to merge."
}
